-- title:
--   Integral j-charts generate the Igusa curve's affine rings
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a $p$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L((q))$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the $X_1(Mp)$ function field, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, together with a compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K$, and let $j \in K$ be a nonzero element whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ with an $A$-algebra structure, $w$ an `IntegralWeightOneForm` over $k$ of level $M$ (a weight-one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ with an integral $q$-expansion whose associated series datum is nonzero over $k$), and let $t$ be an element of the intermediate field [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35) of $k((q))$ whose Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqModC k`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15). For a subset $S$ of a field, `chartRing`/`chartAlg` denotes the subalgebra of elements integral over the subalgebra generated by $S$. The conclusion is a conjunction of two inclusions inside $k((q))$: every $z$ in the Igusa function field that is integral over $k[t]$ has its Laurent series in the $k$-subalgebra generated by all $r$ of the form $\bar{x}/\bar{y}$, where $x, y$ are power series over $A$ with $y$ not reducing to zero modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $b \cdot y = x$ in $L((q))$ for some $b$ integral over $A[j]$ (that is, $b \in$ `chartAlgFin A K j`); and, likewise, every $z$ integral over $k[t^{-1}]$ has its Laurent series in the $k$-subalgebra generated by the analogous quotients $\bar{x}/\bar{y}$ coming from $b$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$ (that is, $b \in$ `chartAlgInf A K j`).
--
--   This is the set-theoretic content of the normality of the reduced multiplicative component of the special fibre of the model of $X(\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_1(p))$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[\zeta_p]$: the two affine rings of the Igusa curve are generated by Gauss reductions of the integral $j$-charts, the statement being phrased entirely on subsets of $k((q))$ so that no reduction map is named. It feeds the surjectivity assertion of [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_surjective_tensorProduct_chartAlg_to_chartRing_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_surjective_tensorProduct_chartAlg_to_chartRing_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_x1_mul) and the transport of that statement along an algebra equivalence.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_chartRing_le_adjoin_gaussReductions_chartAlg_x1_mul.lean

